<title>EGYPT: Abu Qir Fertilisers raises profits.</title>
<headline>Abu Qir Fertilisers raises profits.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1996-09-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Abu Qir Fertilisers and Chemical Industries made 185 million pounds in net after-tax profits available for distribution in the financial year 1995/6, compared to 164.98 million in the previous year, sources close to the company said on Monday. The year ended on June 30.</p>
<p>The company is expected to pay an annual dividend of about 4.00 pounds, against 4.02 pounds the previous year.</p>
<p>The profits are equivalent to 4.89 pounds for each of the 37.8 million shares, which traded at around 41.80 on Monday.</p>
<p>$1 = 3.40 pounds</p>
<p>-- Jonathan Wright +20 2 578 3290/1</p>
</text>
